#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197976 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "804ee2d1-5590-534d-ae11-7d2c5614a9b1" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the Y-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "81b0b6e1-41c3-5329-806e-162b8b27b045" :question/math-academy-id "e-12466" :question/problem "The lamina $D = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\le x \\le y,\\, 0 \\le y \\le 1 \\big\\}$ has the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y) = x^2y$. Find the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nM_y = \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\lambda(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is represented as a type II plane region and\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = x^2y\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM_{y} &= ∬_(D)x \\cdot x^{2}ydA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)x^{3}ydA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{y}x^{3}ydxdy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}y[∫_{0}^{y}x^{3}dx]dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}y \\cdot [\\frac{x^{4}}{4}]_{x = 0}^{x = y}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}y \\cdot \\frac{y^{4}}{4}dy \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}\\frac{y^{5}}{4}dy \\\\\n&= [\\frac{y^{6}}{24}]_{y = 0}^{y = 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{24}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186197977 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "9294903c-1b4c-58b6-a878-7f2220ec763d" :question/math-academy-id "e-12470" :question/problem "A thin plate $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y) = 2x$ is enclosed between the curve $y=1-x^2$ and the $x$-axis for $0 \\leq x \\leq 1$. Find the moment of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "The moment of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\nM_x = \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\lambda(x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nIn our case, $D$ is a type I plane region, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4166/Source/Images/7d803c99f95d817b7da87f748075ad7f.png)\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\le x \\le 1, \\: 0 \\le y \\le 1-x^2 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = 2x\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM_{x} &= ∬_(D)y \\cdot 2xdA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)2xydA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{1 - x^{2}}2xydydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}2x[∫_{0}^{1 - x^{2}}ydy]dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}2x \\cdot [\\frac{y^{2}}{2}]_{y = 0}^{y = 1 - x^{2}}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}x(1 - x^{2})^{2}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}x - 2x^{3} + x^{5}dx \\\\\n&= [\\frac{1}{2}x^{2} - \\frac{1}{2}x^{4} + \\frac{1}{6}x^{6}]_{x = 0}^{x = 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{6} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{6}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198165 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f7a06a8-0260-5b59-b3a5-c02ee03980d4" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Center of Mass of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/id #uuid "8199670b-efe4-537b-8f8a-228d567a0944" :question/math-academy-id "e-8182" :question/problem "Consider a thin plate $D$ that has the mass density function $\\lambda (x,y) = x+y$ and is enclosed between the curve $y=x$ and the $x$-axis for $0 \\leq x \\leq 1$. Given that the mass of the plate is $\\dfrac{1}{2}$ units and its center of mass is located at $(\\overline{x}, \\overline{y})$, what is the value of $\\overline{y}$?" :question/worked-solution "The center of mass of a lamina $D$ with the mass density function $\\lambda(x,y)$ is given by\n\n$$\n(\\overline{x},\\overline{y}) = \\left(\\dfrac{M_y}{m}, \\dfrac{M_x}{m} \\right)\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- $\\displaystyle m = \\iint \\limits_D \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the mass of the lamina,\n- $\\displaystyle M_x = \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $x$-axis, and\n- $\\displaystyle M_y = \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\lambda (x,y) \\: \\textrm{d}A$ is the moment of the lamina about the $y$-axis.\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type I plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4166/Source/Images/00dd64e1a9f10365c732090d6562d731.png)\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\:0 \\le x \\le 1, \\: 0 \\le y \\le x \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\lambda(x,y) = x+y\n$$\n\nSince we require the $y$-coordinate of the center of mass, we need to compute the moment about the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nM_{x} &= ∬_(D)yλ(x, y)dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)y \\cdot (x + y)dA \\\\\n&= ∬_(D)xy + y^{2}dA \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}∫_{0}^{x}xy + y^{2}dydx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}[\\frac{xy^{2}}{2} + \\frac{y^{3}}{3}]_{y = 0}^{y = x}dx \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}(\\frac{x^{3}}{2} + \\frac{x^{3}}{3})dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{6}∫_{0}^{1}x^{3}dx \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{6}[\\frac{1}{4}x^{4}]_{x = 0}^{x = 1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{6}(\\frac{1}{4} - 0) \\\\\n&= \\frac{5}{24}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\overline{y} = \\dfrac{M_x}{m} = \\dfrac{\\left(\\dfrac{5}{24}\\right)}{\\left(\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)} = \\dfrac{5}{12}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198166 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "255c9985-5d85-5fd5-a2b9-c4752f04afac" :knowledge-point/title "Find the Centroid of a Plane Lamina"}] :question/id #uuid "37d7f2ae-90b0-5e6f-83c2-7cb21ed4f089" :question/math-academy-id "e-8183" :question/problem "Consider the thin plate $D$ enclosed between the curve $x=\\sqrt{1-y^2}$ and the $y$-axis for $-1 \\leq y \\leq 1$. Find the $x$-coordinate of its centroid." :question/worked-solution "The centroid of a lamina $D$ with area $A_D$ is given by $(x_c, y_c)$, where\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle x_c = \\dfrac{1}{A_D} \\iint\\limits_D x \\, \\: \\textrm{d}A, \\qquad \\displaystyle y_c = \\dfrac{1}{A_D} \\iint\\limits_D y \\, \\: \\textrm{d}A\n$$\n\nNotice that $D$ is a type II plane region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/4166/Source/Images/d671a38e2ba00f523dee97b36289fe6a.png)\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nD = \\big\\{(x,y) \\:: \\: 0 \\le x \\le \\sqrt{1-y^2}, \\: -1 \\le y \\le 1 \\big\\}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\nA_D = \\dfrac12 \\cdot \\pi\\cdot 1^2 = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-coordinate of the centroid is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{c} &= \\frac{1}{A_{D}}∬_(D)xdA \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{π}∫_{-1}^{1}∫_{0}^{\\sqrt{1 - y^{2}}}xdxdy \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{π}∫_{-1}^{1}[\\frac{x^{2}}{2}]_{x = 0}^{x = \\sqrt{1 - y^{2}}}dy \\\\\n&= \\frac{2}{π}∫_{-1}^{1}\\frac{1 - y^{2}}{2}dy \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{π}∫_{-1}^{1}1 - y^{2}dy \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{π}[y - \\frac{y^{3}}{3}]_{-1}^{1} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{π}[(1 - \\frac{1}{3}) - (-1 + \\frac{1}{3})] \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{π} \\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\\n&= \\frac{4}{3π}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186198556 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "444e9b54-f6d4-5b70-af49-d01556bb3135" :knowledge-point/title "The Moment of a Plane Lamina About the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b8da0ef1-5579-5399-8df3-cc765d4308b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194238} {:answer/id #uuid "064f803f-57fc-5b41-84b4-fa08e0096e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194239} {:answer/id #uuid "43512849-4db1-5c38-8263-249522cd6afa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194240} {:answer/id #uuid "5d3cbb8d-f422-5ee5-8496-5ea357cb898a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194241} {:answer/id #uuid "6c90883d-5cf1-52f1-9ad4-ea88bf615d4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194242}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "064f803f-57fc-5b41-84b4-fa08e0096e53" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186194239} :answer-field/id #uuid "95cc52ea-8c0b-5948-b0d1-2f9b00923bd3" :answer-field/key 